// One line of a response file, the way csc splits one: arguments separated by blanks, and a run
// in double quotes kept whole, blanks and all, with the quotes dropped. A quote may open in the
// middle of an argument and close in the middle of another word: "a b"c is one argument, a bc.
// A quote that never closes runs to the end of the line.
//
// The lines themselves, and the comment lines among them (# first, after any blanks), are told
// apart in ResponseFile.cs: that is a split on line ends, not a grammar.

trivia = none

Line : @string[] = Blank & (Argument & Blank)* & eof

Argument : @string = pieces: Piece+ => @(string.Concat(pieces))

Piece : @string = '"' & text: [^ '"']* & ('"' | eof) => @(text)
                | text: [^ ' ' | '\t' | '"']+       => @(text)

Blank = [' ' | '\t']*

parse Line
